WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:03.044
Reviewer: Last, what this first pass can't tell us.

2
00:00:03.044 --> 00:00:06.084
Reviewer: A screen reader shows whether things work as built,

3
00:00:06.084 --> 00:00:08.767
Reviewer: not whether they help the people they're for.

4
00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:12.999
Reviewer: These need people with disabilities, on their own devices and settings.

5
00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.890
Keyboard: Tab → link, Skip to content

6
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.904
Keyboard: Tab → button, Describe this page

7
00:00:17.904 --> 00:00:19.803
Keyboard: Return → heading, The home page

8
00:00:19.803 --> 00:00:21.558
Tester: First, Describe this page.

9
00:00:21.558 --> 00:00:26.353
Tester: Does a written description of the layout help someone picture the page?

10
00:00:26.353 --> 00:00:28.312
Tester: Is it too long, or too short?

11
00:00:28.312 --> 00:00:32.499
Tester: Blind people who use a screen reader every day should tell us,

12
00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.728
Tester: on VoiceOver and on JAWS or NVDA.

13
00:00:35.457 --> 00:00:37.274
Keyboard: Escape → button, Describe this page

14
00:00:37.274 --> 00:00:40.196
Reviewer: Second, other screen readers and devices.

15
00:00:40.196 --> 00:00:43.048
Reviewer: This pass used VoiceOver in Safari only,

16
00:00:43.048 --> 00:00:48.751
Reviewer: and its biggest finding came from how Safari passes hidden content to VoiceOver.

17
00:00:48.751 --> 00:00:53.599
Reviewer: JAWS, NVDA, VoiceOver on iPhone and TalkBack all behave differently.

18
00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:55.829
Keyboard: Tab → link, Marcelo Paiva

19
00:00:55.829 --> 00:00:57.431
Keyboard: Tab → link, Writing

20
00:00:57.431 --> 00:00:59.042
Keyboard: Tab → link, Work

21
00:00:59.042 --> 00:01:00.660
Keyboard: Tab → link, Signal

22
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.272
Keyboard: Tab → link, Tools

23
00:01:02.272 --> 00:01:03.895
Keyboard: Tab → link, Resume

24
00:01:03.895 --> 00:01:05.506
Keyboard: Tab → button, Set for you, collapsed

25
00:01:05.506 --> 00:01:07.301
Keyboard: Return → button, Set for you, expanded

26
00:01:07.301 --> 00:01:10.455
Tester: Third, Set for you reads its settings as a sentence.

27
00:01:10.455 --> 00:01:14.883
Tester: Whether that feels natural, and whether the new announcements are enough,

28
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:19.676
Tester: is for screen reader users, and people with cognitive or learning disabilities,

29
00:01:19.676 --> 00:01:20.101
Tester: to say.

30
00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.518
Keyboard: Escape → button, Set for you, collapsed

31
00:01:22.518 --> 00:01:27.795
Reviewer: Fourth, motion. The drawings drift and the background moves. The pause button works…

32
00:01:27.795 --> 00:01:32.067
Reviewer: but is it found in time, and is the motion comfortable before it is?

33
00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:34.893
Reviewer: People with vestibular disorders can tell us.

34
00:01:35.524 --> 00:01:37.700
Keyboard: Command-Plus: zooms the page

35
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.952
Keyboard: Command-Plus: zooms the page

36
00:01:39.952 --> 00:01:41.911
Keyboard: Command-Plus: zooms the page

37
00:01:41.911 --> 00:01:43.981
Tester: Fifth, zoom and magnification.

38
00:01:43.981 --> 00:01:49.365
Tester: Zoomed in, the header stays at the top, and some text sits over moving colour.

39
00:01:49.365 --> 00:01:54.335
Tester: People with low vision who use zoom or a screen magnifier should try it.

40
00:01:54.956 --> 00:01:56.938
Keyboard: Command-0: back to actual size

41
00:01:56.938 --> 00:01:59.368
Reviewer: Sixth, voice control and switch access.

42
00:01:59.368 --> 00:02:04.353
Reviewer: Names were checked for what a screen reader says, not for what people say aloud,

43
00:02:04.353 --> 00:02:09.463
Reviewer: and the home page has more than fifty stops for someone moving one step at a time.

44
00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:12.112
Keyboard: Return → button, Set for you, expanded

45
00:02:12.112 --> 00:02:13.725
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Drawings, in calm color

46
00:02:13.725 --> 00:02:15.308
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Theme, following my device

47
00:02:15.308 --> 00:02:16.930
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Motion, allowed

48
00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:18.548
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Home page, a list of essays

49
00:02:18.548 --> 00:02:20.048
Keyboard: Focus is on → pop-up button, Home page, a list of essays

50
00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:24.929
Tester: And last, the collage. Set for you can turn the home page into a field of drawings.

51
00:02:24.929 --> 00:02:26.954
Tester: This pass tested the list only.

52
00:02:27.576 --> 00:02:29.391
Keyboard: Escape → button, Set for you, collapsed

53
00:02:29.391 --> 00:02:31.630
Tester: That's the end of the first pass.

54
00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:36.516
Tester: Six problems found on the page: five fixed and live, and one still open.

55
00:02:36.916 --> 00:02:39.041
Reviewer: The next test is with people.
